## Overall Summary  

2025 was normal-to-dry across the MSEP watershed, with annual total precipitation within 5% of the 30-year average in 5 of the 14 subbasins, and 10-20% lower than normal in the other 9 subbasins. The subbasins that were driest were generally in the southern portions of the watershed, whereas the more northern subbasins were closer to the long-term average. See @fig-mapPrcpTotalAndAnomPct and @fig-precipPctDiff in particular for details.    


